WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.840
China's factory activity contracted in July, with the official purchasing manager's index falling below the 50 point threshold that separates growth from contraction. New orders and output both declined, pointing to weaker domestic and export demand at a time when global trade faces ongoing uncertainty from tariffs and shifting supply chains. Separate private sector surveys had already signaled similar softness in manufacturing before the official release.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:39.980
Reuters reported the contraction as unexpected and tied to faltering demand, framing it as a signal that China's post-pandemic recovery remains fragile after earlier stimulus rounds.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:50.800
Chinese state media have emphasized external pressures such as trade restrictions while highlighting government stimulus measures already in place to support industrial output.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:01:01.800
Economists at international banks note that the reading aligns with earlier private sector surveys showing similar weakness in manufacturing, particularly in export-oriented sectors.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:09.960
The data also coincide with reports of softer global commodity prices that often track Chinese industrial demand.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:24.120
What happens next? Analysts will watch the next monthly reading and any additional stimulus announcements to gauge whether the weakness spreads further into employment and investment, shifting now to a developing story in Africa.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:34.540
A rights group reported that forces from Russia's Africa Core carried out an attack in Mali that killed civilians in what it described as an indiscriminate operation.

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:50.560
The incident adds to concerns about the conduct of Russian-linked forces operating in the Sahel region. Reuters cited the rights groups' documentation of the attack, including witness accounts of civilian casualties and the use of unguided munitions.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:58.920
Russian officials have previously described their Africa Core presence as support for partner governments against insurgencies in the region.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:09.060
Sahel-based analysts point to the broader pattern of foreign forces filling security gaps left by earlier international withdrawals from Mali and neighboring states.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:13.180
Local authorities have not yet issued a detailed public response.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:24.840
Next, a statement from Hamas on Disarmament in Gaza. Hamas stated it would disarm in Gaza following an announcement by former President Trump of a proposed board of peace plan.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:31.040
The announcement was issued through Hamas media channels and referenced the proposed governance structure.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:43.720
BBC News reported the Hamas announcement and noted the absence of an immediate Israeli response, placing it within the wider sequence of truce proposals that have circulated since earlier this year.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:51.760
Palestinian officials have framed the move as a potential step toward ending the current conflict and allowing reconstruction to begin.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:03:00.780
Israeli security analysts stressed that any disarmament would require verifiable implementation mechanisms and third party oversight.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:09.480
US officials involved in the plan have described it as an attempt to create new governance structures that could replace existing arrangements in Gaza.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:24.800
One position holds that Hamas's stated willingness to disarm reflects a pragmatic recognition that continued armed confrontation has become unsustainable for Gaza's population and that external oversight could provide a path to reconstruction.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:38.880
The strongest version of this view emphasizes that verifiable steps toward demilitarization would reduce the risk of renewed cycles of violence and allow resources to shift toward civilian needs such as housing and infrastructure.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:51.940
A competing position maintains that disarmament without ironclad security guarantees for Israel would leave the country exposed to future attacks given Hamas's past record of rearming after previous agreements.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:04:00.860
Advocates of this view argue that any plan must first establish independent monitoring and border controls before weapons are relinquished.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:08.280
Israel has not yet commented on the statement, meanwhile a large migrant crossing occurred at the Sudah border.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:20.860
Officials estimate that about 49,000 migrants entered the Spanish enclave of Siyuta from Morocco over a 24-hour period, with at least 18 deaths reported during the attempts.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:32.800
AP News documented the death toll and the rapid influx, noting the involvement of Moroccan and Spanish border forces in managing the crossings at multiple points along the frontier.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:43.220
Spanish government statements have focused on the logistical strain on Siyuta's infrastructure and the need for coordinated EU level responses to share responsibility.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:51.240
Moroccan officials have described the flows as driven by economic hardship and instability in origin countries further south.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:57.200
The episode marks one of the largest single-day movements recorded at the enclave in recent years.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.380
Spanish local authorities have requested additional support from the national government.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:07.040
In currency markets, the Indian rupee strengthened to a three-week high.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:14.040
The gain was supported by purchases from state-run banks, lower oil prices, and a weaker US dollar.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:23.400
Reuters attributed the gain to coordinated buying by public sector banks and softer energy prices that reduced import pressure on the current account.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:30.900
Indian exporters have welcomed the firmer currency for reducing import costs on capital goods and intermediate inputs.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:38.200
Importors note it may ease pressure on raw material purchases and help contain inflation in consumer goods.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:44.300
The Reserve Bank of India's interventions have helped stabilize sentiment in currency markets.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:49.020
Traders are watching for further moves in global oil and dollar trends.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:54.140
South Korea's Cosby Index rose nearly 18% in a single day.

00:05:54.140 --> 00:06:00.980
The gain was its biggest on record and came as AI-related stocks recovered from earlier sharp losses.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:10.540
AP News linked the jump to renewed investor interest in semiconductor and AI companies after recent sell-offs driven by global rate concerns.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:18.800
Korean financial regulators have noted the importance of orderly trading during such swings to prevent excessive leverage build-up.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:30.420
Global fund managers have cited improving sentiment around artificial intelligence supply chains as a contributing factor to the broad-based rally across chip makers and related suppliers.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:35.240
Market participants are monitoring whether the surge holds in coming sessions.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:48.160
Now, some progress worth knowing about. Investigators identified one of the world's largest illegal gambling operations routing hundreds of millions of dollars in cryptocurrency through an office in Dubai.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:53.340
As part of a broader $4 billion Iranian sanctions evasion scheme.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:58.520
Reuters documented the network's structure and its connection to sanctions circumvention,

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:04.180
drawing on transaction records and corporate filings that traced funds across several continents.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:13.780
Financial crime specialists have pointed to the use of crypto as a way to move value outside conventional banking channels that are subject to stricter reporting.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:22.940
Dubai regulators have stated they are cooperating with international inquiries into the matter and reviewing licensing rules for crypto service providers.

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:27.200
Authorities in multiple jurisdictions are now reviewing the evidence.

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:32.420
Now, to really understand this story, there's something most coverage leaves out.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:39.300
Most coverage of factory slowdowns treats the monthly purchasing managers index as a simple up-or-down signal.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:50.340
Yet, the index is built from a survey of purchasing managers who answer questions about new orders, output, employment, and inventories on a scale that produces a single diffusion number.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:58.100
When the headline figure drops below 50, it means more firms reported contraction than expansion in the previous month.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:07.460
But the underlying components can move in different directions, revealing whether weakness is concentrated in exports, domestic demand, or hiring plans.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:21.420
The survey is conducted by a private firm in many countries and by official statistical agencies and others, so timing, sample size, and seasonal adjustments differ and can produce conflicting readings even for the same economy.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:29.600
In China, the official version draws from a larger state-linked sample while a separate private gauge often shows sharper swings.

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:45.220
Knowing this, when you hear a single PMI number cited as proof of recession or recovery, you can check whether the sub indices for new orders and employment moved in the same direction, and whether the survey method matches the one used in prior months.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:58.940
The concrete thing to verify next time is whether the reporting agency publishes the full component breakdown and the response rate for that month's survey so readers can judge how representative the headline number actually is.

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:06.700
If you want to go deeper on China's factory slowdown, compare how Reuters and AP news are covering today's lead story.

